## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about I/O efficiency, batching, and dynamic graph algorithms under memory constraints; blends theory with practical concerns like latency and cache locality.

## Key Concepts

- External memory I/O model (M, B) and batch updates
- Dynamic connectivity with batched insertions
- Amortized analysis and rebuild strategies
- Spanning forests and residual edges
- Locality-aware data partitioning

## Code Example

